    "brief": {
      "text": "SITUATION NOW\nCôte d'Ivoire became the newest signatory of the Artemis Accords, as announced by NASA. [2]\nWaraba Gold confirmed in-situ gold mineralisation at Fetiko within a 1.9 kilometre gold-in-saprolite corridor at the Tengrela Gold Project in Côte d'Ivoire. [3]\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR CÔTE D’IVOIRE\nCôte d'Ivoire's signing of the Artemis Accords signals its growing engagement in space exploration, while the country faces 7 US OFAC and Canada SEMA sanctions designations that may complicate international partnerships. [2][E2]\n\nWATCH ITEMS\nThe outcome of the Zipline expansion to ten centres in Côte d'Ivoire over eight years remains to be seen. [4]",
